-- Migration: sync_prod_schema_to_contract_uuid_user_ids
-- Takes prod (wntgnjrrzfndunqaiobo) from its hand-edited state to the contract on
-- branch feat/uuid-user-ids (storageHash below). Generated with `prisma db update --dry-run`
-- against a local prod-like copy, then edited:
--   * users.user_id is RENAMED to id (planner wanted drop + add, which would lose rows)
--   * owner_id FKs are kept (they follow the rename) instead of drop + re-add
--   * users.id loses its auth.uid() default (contract has none)
--   * the legacy per-user RLS policies are dropped; RLS stays ENABLED on every table
--     (contract declares @@rls on every model; app connects as postgres, which bypasses RLS)
--   * sync_user_email_from_auth() keeps working (it already filters on id)
--   * Prisma contract marker updated like `prisma db update` does
-- apply_migration wraps this in one transaction.
